From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 14:04:17 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 173/207] runner: stream each cell record as it lands, so a cut
 stream keeps a record per write

A reply cut before its final chunk (a client deadline or close) had no runner records: they came only in the
finished receipt. The lane host now sends each record new or grown since its last send (Event.cells, from
runner_receipt.notes) ahead of the tokens that land it. The server keeps each record's versions until a newer
one is fully shown and streams, beside the choices as tensorfold.runner.cells (live: true), the records whose
landed bytes the client already has, never fewer than it sent. The finished receipt is unchanged; with records
off no note is made and the stream is byte for byte as before.

(cherry picked from commit 05aa3debe4e893baf904b548e32ba7a24238f39c)
